=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
A thorough end-to-end investigation of the dc_clos_bgp fabric finds no fault.
Both directions of the reported path (pc_0_0 10.0.0.2 → pc_0_1 10.0.1.2 and
the reverse) complete with zero packet loss and ~1–1.5 ms RTT, confirming
the data plane is intact.

On the control plane, every BGP session in the fabric is in the Established
state: super_spine_router_0 (AS 65000) peers correctly with both
spine_router_0_0 (AS 65100) and spine_router_0_1 (AS 65101); each spine peers
with both leaf routers; and each leaf has a session to both spines. All five
routers carry the two host prefixes (10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24) in their
RIBs and FIBs, and both leaf routers hold a primary path via spine_router_0_0
plus a hot-standby path via spine_router_0_1 — so single-spine redundancy is
also intact.

The only surface-level anomaly — spine_router_0_0 showing PfxRcd = 0 from
super_spine — is expected, correct BGP behaviour: super_spine's best paths for
both prefixes arrived from spine_router_0_0's own AS (65100), so when it
re-advertises them the AS path contains 65100 and spine_router_0_0 rightfully
rejects them to prevent loops. All other devices have the correct number of
received prefixes. All physical interfaces are UP across every router.

Root cause: There is no fault. The user's ticket describes a symptom that is
not reproducible in the current lab state; the fabric is fully healthy and no
configuration change or corrective action is required.
=== END ===
```